```
Hmm, constructing a full observation is heavy. Better: use seededStore, then overwrite `lastRefreshAt` deletion, and also refresh the observations' observedAt to "now" so it's deterministic:

```js
test('board freshness falls back to the newest observation when the completed-refresh marker is missing', async () => {
  const store = await seededStore();
  const recent = new Date(Date.now() - 60 * 60 * 1000).toISOString();
  for (const row of await store.listObservations()) {
    if (row.observedAt) await store.putObservation({ ...row, observedAt: recent });
  }
  await store.setMeta('lastRefreshAt', null);
  const board = await (await worker.fetch(new Request('https://example.test/api/board?grams=500&dest=tel-aviv'), envWith(store), {})).json();
  assert.equal(board.freshness.lastRefreshAt, null);
  assert.equal(board.freshness.lastObservationAt, recent);
  assert.equal(board.freshness.stale, false, 'fresh saved offers must not read as never-refreshed');
  assert.ok(board.freshness.ageHours <= 1.1);
  assert.equal(board.freshness.dataAsOf, recent);
});
```
Note: memory store putObservation stores row as is; snapshot returns them. listObservations includes attempt markers with observedAt null; skipping those. Also note seededStore's run set vendor states; irrelevant.

