docs/SOURCES.md:46:**Versioned policy promotion and staleness (iterations 3-73, 3-76 and 3-77):** a validated quote is promoted by hand into `src/lib/policies.js` as a versioned policy (vendor, product/SKU scope, service, destination scope, amount or free-shipping rule with the vendor's `above`/`at_least` wording, secondary delivery alternatives, evidence URL and retrieval time, `reviewBy`). The read-time evaluator in the same module enriches an observation whose own shipping is unknown, never overwrites a fresher parsed rate, treats conflicting policies as `inconsistent`, and stops applying a policy once `reviewBy` passes (the offer then shows explicit unknown shipping again). Four policies are checked in: Pucks' ₪30 / free-above-₪100 rule is `pucks-il-home-delivery` v1, observed 2026-10-12T18:10:10Z; CoffeeMan's published ₪25 single/4-pack rule is `coffeeman-single-4pack-il-home-delivery` v2 with the cart-observed ₪15 distribution-center alternative and the cart-observed free condition (free home courier from the lowest observed free ₪231 item subtotal; a ₪198 cart was charged ₪25, so the condition carries `freeThresholdOrigin: observed_cart` and its own evidence from 2026-10-12T20:09:00Z); CoffeeMan's ₪20 one-8-pack (2 kg) checkout quote is `coffeeman-8pack-il-cart-quote` v1, observed 2026-10-12T20:07:00Z and scoped to the 8-pack offer URL with `maxTotalGrams: 2000`, no free threshold and the observed ₪20 distribution-center alternative; Coffee4U's published ₪30 door-to-door rule is `coffee4u-il-home-delivery` v1 with the ₪15 pickup-point alternative and the observed closed-locality-list coverage shape (observed 2026-10-12T20:25:00Z). All carry `reviewBy` 2026-11-11; re-checking the rendered estimator or the product page renews the evidence and version, and `/api/status` exposes the current version, service, alternative ids, observation time and review date. Each policy is also the adapter's single source for the researched values it describes, so the parsed row, the read-time evaluator and the tests share one representation. Enrichment never changes the offer's price/stock observation time or the refresh completion marker. Since iteration 3-78 the adapters honor the same review window at parse time (`policyIsCurrent()`): once a policy is past its review date, its researched rate and any policy-derived alternative are withheld, so a freshly parsed offer falls back to explicit unknown shipping instead of carrying a stale quote; page-published rates (CoffeeMan's ₪25, Coffee4U's ₪30/₪15) stay because they are parsed from the vendor page, not from the policy.
